# conformance/vibenvm/normalise.rules — every normalisation the comparison
# applies, declared in one file (PROP-075 `#VIBENVM-SUITE`).
#
# The comparison is of observation records, field by field. Two tools cannot
# agree on absolute paths, on the colours a terminal gets or on how long a
# download took, and they are not asked to: those differences are erased here,
# mechanically and visibly, and nothing else is. An LLM is nowhere in this
# file, which is the point of it.
#
# Rows are tab-separated:
#   value  <sed expression>   applied, in order, to every field of every
#                             observation record (`observe.sh` builds a
#                             `sed -E` script out of these rows)
#   drop   <ERE>              a stdout/stderr line matching it is dropped
#                             before a case with `compare_stdout = true` is
#                             compared; it never affects a record field
#   sort   <field>            that field is a set, not a sequence: its
#                             members are sorted before comparison
#
# Placeholders are substituted with the sandbox's own values at run time, so
# one rule covers both sandboxes:
#   @HOME@      the sandbox's HOME
#   @TOOLROOT@  the root the tool under test owns ($NVM_DIR for sandbox A,
#               the vibe settings/install root for sandbox B)
#   @MIRROR@    the loopback mirror's base URL
#   @TMPDIR@    the sandbox's TMPDIR

# --- paths ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The tool root first: it lives under HOME, so the more specific rule wins.
value	s|@TOOLROOT@|<TOOLROOT>|g
value	s|@TMPDIR@|<TMPDIR>|g
value	s|@HOME@|<HOME>|g
value	s|@MIRROR@|<MIRROR>|g

# One version-manager lays its versions out as `versions/node/v22.9.0`, the
# next as `apps/node/org.vibevm.node.node@22.9.0`; that is a layout, not an
# observable. Any path under the tool root collapses to `<TOOLROOT>@v<version>`
# plus whatever the tool puts after it, so `which_node` and `owned_path`
# compare as what they are — the directory of a specific version — without
# either layout winning. The version may be a path component of its own
# (`/v22.9.0`, nvm) or the version half of a coordinate (`@22.9.0`, vibe):
# both separators end the part that is layout.
value	s|<TOOLROOT>[^,;=]*[/@]v?([0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+([-+][0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?)|<TOOLROOT>@v\1|g

# --- how a version is spelled --------------------------------------------
# nvm writes a version `v22.9.0` and vibe writes it `22.9.0`. The `v` is a
# spelling and not an observable — nvm's own `nvm_version` adds and strips
# it freely, and `.nvmrc` is read either way — so a leading `v` is dropped
# wherever a version starts a field or a member of one. The tool-root rule
# above has already produced `<TOOLROOT>@v…`, whose `v` is part of that
# placeholder and is left alone because `@` is not a member separator.
value	s/(^|[,;=|[:space:]])v([0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+)/\1\2/g

# --- colour and timing ---------------------------------------------------
value	s/\x1B\[[0-9;?]*[a-zA-Z]//g
value	s/[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?(ms|s)([^a-zA-Z0-9]|$)/<T>\3/g

# --- stdout lines a comparison may not depend on -------------------------
# Download progress (curl's bar and nvm's own hashes), npm's notices and
# funding chatter, and nvm's "Now using"/"Downloading" progress noise carry
# no state: the observation record already says what happened.
drop	^[[:space:]]*#+[[:space:]]*$
drop	^[[:space:]]*[0-9.]+%.*$
drop	^[[:space:]]*%[[:space:]]+Total.*$
drop	^[[:space:]]*Dload[[:space:]]+Upload.*$
drop	^npm (notice|warn|WARN|ERR!) .*$
drop	^[[:space:]]*$
drop	^[0-9]+ packages are looking for funding$
drop	^[[:space:]]*run `npm fund` for details$
drop	^Computing checksum with sha256sum$
drop	^Checksums matched!$
drop	^Downloading and installing node v.*\.\.\.$
drop	^Downloading https?://.*$

# --- fields that are sets, not sequences ---------------------------------
sort	installed
sort	aliases
sort	globals
